  - zero-free region
  - quasi-Riemann hypothesis
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - Comparator
abstract: >-
  OpenAI's kernel-checked theorem that the Riemann zeta function has no zero with real part greater than 7/8
  is composed with de Bruijn's 1950 heat-flow theorem, as formalized on the Arda dbn island, in a single Lean 4
  environment at OpenAI's Mathlib pin. The result, every zero of H_t is real for every t >= 9/32, is classically
  Lambda <= 9/32 for the de Bruijn-Newman constant: the first bound below de Bruijn's 1/2 that is machine-checked
  end to end, re-checked by a second kernel (nanoda, via Comparator), independently audited and judged against a
  registered statement. It is weaker than the numerical bounds 0.22 and 0.2, and it is not the Riemann Hypothesis.
